# Lines the code page test (codepage.bat) must write to COM1 with
# COUNTRY=049,850, DISPLAY.SYS CON=(EGA,437,2) and NLSFUNC from INSTALL=
# (scripts/smoke-test): a German setup. DOS's code page is 850 from boot,
# CON's none until MODE selects one, and CHCP finds NLSFUNC loaded. The
# rest is as with DISPLAY.SYS alone (tests/codepage/ega/expect), which
# says how the font lines are checked.

^GRDOS-TEST-BEGIN$

# At boot DISPLAY.SYS has the hardware code page and two places for
# prepared ones, and no code page selected: CON's query fails (5) and the
# font is the BIOS'
^== BOOT$
^CON CODEPAGE ERROR 5$
^FONT 9B (?!00 00 00 00 00 7C C[6E] )[0-9A-F]{2}( [0-9A-F]{2}){15}$
^FONT D5 00 00 00 00 00 1F 18 1F 18 18 18 18 18 18 18 18$
^No code page has been selected$
^Hardware code pages:$
^  code page 437$
^Prepared code pages:$
^  code page not prepared$
^  code page not prepared$
^MODE status code page function completed$

# 850 and 865 from EGA.CPI
^== PREPARE$
^MODE prepare code page function completed$
^No code page has been selected$
^Hardware code pages:$
^  code page 437$
^Prepared code pages:$
^  code page 850$
^  code page 865$
^MODE status code page function completed$

# Selecting 850 loads its font
^== SELECT$
^MODE select code page function completed$
^CON CODEPAGE 850$
^FONT 9B 00 00 00 00 00 7C CE DE F6 E6 C6 7C 00 00 00 00$
^FONT D5 00 00 00 00 00 38 18 18 18 18 18 3C 00 00 00 00$

# KEYB GR takes CON's code page; Germany's layout has 437 and 850, not
# the prepared 865, which KEYB says
^== KEYB$
^One or more CON code pages invalid for given keyboard code$
^Current keyboard code: GR  code page: 850$
^Current CON code page: 850$

# NLSFUNC is resident already; DOS's code page is 850; CHCP switches CON
# with DOS: 437, the hardware's font, with KEYB following, then 850 again
^== CHCP$
^NLSFUNC already installed$
^Active code page: 850$
^CON CODEPAGE 437$
^FONT 9B (?!00 00 00 00 00 7C C[6E] )[0-9A-F]{2}( [0-9A-F]{2}){15}$
^FONT D5 00 00 00 00 00 1F 18 1F 18 18 18 18 18 18 18 18$
^Current keyboard code: GR  code page: 437$
^Current CON code page: 437$
^CON CODEPAGE 850$
^FONT 9B 00 00 00 00 00 7C CE DE F6 E6 C6 7C 00 00 00 00$
^FONT D5 00 00 00 00 00 38 18 18 18 18 18 3C 00 00 00 00$

# A video mode set (MODE CO80) loads the selected code page's font again
^== MODE$
^CON CODEPAGE 850$
^FONT 9B 00 00 00 00 00 7C CE DE F6 E6 C6 7C 00 00 00 00$
^FONT D5 00 00 00 00 00 38 18 18 18 18 18 3C 00 00 00 00$

# MODE selects 865, which KEYB GR has no table for (it keeps 850's); CHCP
# refuses 865, which COUNTRY.SYS does not have for Germany; 860
# is not prepared; LCD.CPI has no EGA fonts, and EGA.CPI no code page 999,
# which DISPLAY.SYS reports as an invalid font file; a missing file;
# REFRESH loads 865 again. CON is left in 865, with its font.
^== ERRORS$
^Current keyboard does not support this code page$
^Invalid code page$
^Code page not prepared$
^Font file contents invalid$
^Device error during prepare$
^Font file contents invalid$
^Device error during prepare$
^Failure to access code page font file$
^Current keyboard does not support this code page$
^CON CODEPAGE 865$
^FONT 9B 00 00 00 00 00 7C C6 CE D6 E6 C6 7C 00 00 00 00$
^FONT D5 00 00 00 00 00 1F 18 1F 18 18 18 18 18 18 18 18$
^GRDOS-TEST-END$
